sequenceDiagram
  box rgb(237, 242, 247) OCC trusted process
    participant M as Management service
    participant C as OCC authority
    participant F as Forwarder library
  end
  box rgb(235, 243, 240) OpenShell
    participant L as Storage / refresh owner
  end
  participant P as Provider
  Note over M,P: Proposed MVP placement, generic contracts allow later services / workers
  M->>F: Capture authenticated caller / user and business operation
  F-->>M: Sealed OperationHandle
  M->>C: Authorize captured operation, exact source / grant and preparation purpose
  C-->>M: Preparation Permit or refusal
  break Denied or authority unavailable
    Note over M,C: Refuse before material access
  end
  M->>L: prepare(Preparation, Command)
  Note over M,L: Same fenced owner, owner authorizes issuer I/O<br/>Agent / bootstrap cannot select preparation
  L-->>M: Change of LifecycleStatus
  break Failed, uncertain, withdrawn or too late
    Note over M,L: Preserve operation and cleanup, inspect / reconcile, no blind replay
  end
  M->>F: forward captured business operation after preparation
  F->>C: EgressAuthorizer.check(before_access)
  C-->>F: AccessPermit or Refusal
  break Denied or authority unavailable
    F-->>M: Refuse before resolution
  end
  F->>L: CredentialResolver.resolve calls readWarm with AccessPermit
  L-->>F: Committed candidate, Resolver binds MaterialEvidence or refuses
  break Material refused or unavailable
    F-->>M: Refuse without a send permit
  end
  Note over F,L: No request-path issuance, storage / refresh remains in OpenShell
  Note over M,F: Access token transient inside trusted OCC sender only
  F->>C: EgressAuthorizer.check(before_send)<br/>Actual operation + MaterialEvidence
  C-->>F: SendPermit or Refusal
  alt Both checks allow and material usable within original deadline
    F->>P: Inject and send once
    P-->>F: Provider response
    F->>F: Apply registered response policy
    F-->>M: SafeResponse or blocked / uncertain outcome
    M->>M: Return sanitized metadata only
  else Denied, unavailable, unusable or too late
    F-->>M: Refuse before dispatch
  end
  Note over M,P: Roots stay with owner / issuer, never handed to management callers<br/>Internal material callbacks only, no tokens / handles to Agent or UI<br/>No automatic retry after possible dispatch
